\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The CPSolver iteration loop. The incumbent $\sigma $ is updated only when the comparator judges the new solution better. Section\nobreakspace {}\ref {sec:rl} substitutes only the \emph {Propose move} step.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Schema of the Taasika scheduling database, the source of the pipeline.\relax }}{9}{figure.caption.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The taasika-v3 pipeline. Data flows left to right and top to bottom; the dashed return path is the refinement loop described in Section\nobreakspace {}\ref {sec:evaluation}.\relax }}{10}{figure.caption.5}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The iterative workflow adopted during the phase. Only the \emph {Analyse} step is manual; every other transition is a scripted command.\relax }}{17}{figure.caption.15}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Student violation rate against the student-conflict weight, on a fixed instance with a 900-second budget and three seeds per weight. Every weight at or above 0.5 improves on the stock B0 configuration, and seed-to-seed variance is comparable to the effect size.\relax }}{18}{figure.caption.18}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Hard-check pass rates of the final solution (term Spr11 solution scored against the Spr12 dataset). The vertical axis starts at 85\,\% to make the three non-perfect checks legible.\relax }}{19}{figure.caption.21}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Training and production configurations of the learning layer. During training, Python drives several resident JVM workers over gRPC; in production the frozen policy runs inside the solver's own JVM with a fallback path.\relax }}{22}{figure.caption.29}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces System architecture. The generators turn a Taasika snapshot into Data Exchange XML; the UniTime server and the headless module both solve against it; the evaluator scores the result against the same XML rather than against the solver.\relax }}{24}{figure.caption.37}%
